"An old light bulb works by making a thin wire so hot that it glows, and most of its energy is lost as heat. An LED turns electricity into light directly, so it uses less power, makes less waste heat, and lasts longer. The next time you switch on a lamp, remember: you are using a semiconductor.": "35207f97b380",
