"Red LEDs came first, in the 1960s. Blue was much harder, and it took until the early 1990s. That mattered a great deal. With red, green, and blue together, a screen can show every color. And a blue LED covered with a yellow material called phosphor gives white light, the kind that now lights our homes.": "4a524646eaa0",
